  "grammar": [
    "<b>Imperative of √i 'go':</b> <span class='dv'>विनोदम् एतु</span> 'may it go to joy', meaning 'may it find joy'. A tiny verb: एति (goes), एतु (may it go).",
    "<b>Consonant sandhi:</b> <span class='dv'>दिक् + अम्बर → दिगम्बर</span>. A hard consonant softens before a vowel, like वेगात् → वेगाद् in the bamboo verse.",
    "<b>Root √rudh:</b> <span class='dv'>निरुद्ध</span> 'blocked'. One root gives निरुद्ध (blocked), प्रतिरोध (resistance) and अवरोध (obstruction)."
